@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# Metric naming
+
+Public counters use lowercase names with standard TRex TCP/UDP prefixes.
+Discover counter IDs and descriptions through the API; do not hard-code IDs.
+
+| Prefix | Measurement |
+|---|---|
+| `tcps_ttfb_*` | Connection time to first response byte |
+| `tcps_ttlb_*` | Connection time to last response byte |
+| `tcps_http_req_ttfb_*` | HTTP request time to first response byte |
+| `tcps_http_req_ttlb_*` | HTTP request time to last response byte |
+| `udps_rtt_*` | UDP transaction round-trip time |
+| `tcps_tls_version_*` | Negotiated TLS version |
+| `tcps_tls_cipher_*` | Negotiated cipher suite |
+| `tcps_tls_group_*` | Negotiated key exchange group |
+| `tcps_tls_peer_signature_*` | Peer signature algorithm |
+
+Latency sample totals use the `count` suffix. Cipher/group suffixes are lowercase,
+for example `tcps_tls_cipher_tls_aes_128_gcm_sha256` and `tcps_tls_group_x25519`.
+Detailed distributions and TLS parameters are available through `get_stats()`;
+the terminal table exposes a smaller set for readability.
+
+Nested scheduler and TLS cost diagnostics in `get_util_stats()` have their own
+scope and are not TCP/UDP traffic counters.
