+++ b/doc/astf-native-tls.md
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# Native TLS for ASTF
+
+The RFC 9411 extension integrates AWS-LC TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3 into TRex's
+ASTF TCP/DPDK path. Both endpoints perform real handshakes and exchange
+authenticated application data. TLS is opt-in per ASTF program.
+
+Each flow owns its TLS state and bounded BIO buffers on its DP worker.
+The TCP adapter feeds ordered ciphertext, handles partial records and
+backpressure, and queues encrypted output through the existing mbuf path.
+Certificate, protocol and resource failures close the affected flow.
+There is no external proxy or separate crypto process.
+
+## Configuration and operation
+
+- [TLS policy and mutual authentication](astf-tls-policy.md)
+- [HTTP response validation and measurements](astf-http-validation.md)
+- [HTTP/2, including cleartext prior knowledge](astf-http2.md)
+- [Receive timestamp attribution](astf-rx-timestamps.md)
+- [Build dependencies](astf-build-dependencies.md)
+- [Validation commands](astf-tls-validation.md)
+- [Cost diagnostics](astf-cost-metrics.md)
+
+Use the repository's getting-started guide to apply the complete patch series
+to the pinned TRex source and build with `--rfc9411`.
+
+TLS capability alone does not establish RFC 9411 benchmark compliance. Workload,
+DUT configuration, measurement procedure and reported results also matter.
+Throughput and timestamp accuracy require validation on the target NIC and host.
